The original FinRL-X source tree is preserved unmodified under legacy/finrlx/ (upstream commit
4409abe). The following MarketIQ files are adapted from FinRL-X and carry an attribution header:

  marketiq/config/settings.py          <- src/config/settings.py (pydantic-settings pattern)
  marketiq/data/calendar.py            <- src/data/trading_calendar.py
  marketiq/data/models.py              <- src/data/data_store.py (schema concepts)
  marketiq/data/providers/fmp.py       <- src/data/data_fetcher.py (FMP endpoints, incremental fetch)
  marketiq/analysis/sentiment.py       <- src/data/data_fetcher.py (OpenAI sentiment classifier)
  marketiq/backtest/metrics.py         <- src/backtest/backtest_engine.py, src/trading/performance_analyzer.py
  marketiq/backtest/walk_forward.py    <- src/strategies/adaptive_rotation/walk_forward.py (pattern)
  marketiq/paper/alpaca_adapter.py     <- src/trading/alpaca_manager.py

The bundled dataset data/finrl_trading.7z (daily prices and FMP quarterly statements) is distributed
by the FinRL-Trading repository. FinRL-X paper: Yang, Zhang, She, Liao, Zhang, "FinRL-X: An AI-Native
Modular Infrastructure for Quantitative Trading", DMO-FinTech workshop at PAKDD 2026, arXiv:2603.21330.

